  "diagnosis": {
    "status": "confirmed stale TypeSpec marker lifetime in frozen source; proposed one-line correction not executed",
    "productDefect": "TypeSpecifications.load keeps its active metadata-specification marker in the operation passed into semantic graph completion, although that TypeSpec signature has already resolved to a canonical TypeDesc.",
    "mechanism": [
      "A nongeneric C initially starts ordinary nominal completion before generic closure has been activated.",
      "C.InterfaceImpl names TypeSpec S encoding I<C>. load(S) creates a scoped active marker and resolves its signature to canonical I<C>.",
      "The finished signature calls complete(I<C>, nested), where nested still contains S.",
      "Completing I<C> activates finite closure. The closure follows the C actual argument, then reads C's direct InterfaceImpl record.",
      "That identity-only read of S encounters the stale marker and throws Circular TypeSpec resolution even though the earlier signature read is no longer active."
    ],
    "observedStackAgreement": "Both retained TypeLoad failures pass through TypeSpecifications.load line38, TypeLoader.#closureTemplate and the InterfaceImpl fallback in TypeDefinitionCompletion. The combined closure.test loops acyclic-expansion and non-generic-self-interface without annotating the individual throw, and native replay likewise does not wrap successful-operation throws with case ID; do not assert an individually instrumented failing case.",
    "independentNativeDecision": "The separate native observer returned the non-generic self-interface definition successfully, as well as the acyclic-expansion controls. Actual raw native output remains authoritative.",
    "proposedCorrection": "After await signature(module, specification.signature, nested), pass the incoming operation to semantic complete(type, operation). Keep the nested marker through signature binding only. Preserve the identityOnly branch and every other operation field.",
    "preservedGuards": [
      "Direct TypeSpec S->S and mutual S->T->S recursion still reenter while signature binding has its active marker.",
      "Incoming nominal inheritance path stays intact; this is not resetting the full ancestry.",
      "Scoped marker identities and work charging remain unchanged.",
      "Encoded category obligations still accumulate on the same root during signature resolution.",
      "Erased nominal cycles and expanding formal SCCs continue through their independent current checks.",
      "No resolved TypeSpec-result cache or shared pending promise is introduced."
    ],
    "qualificationRequired": [
      "Dedicated source test for plain C:I<C> requested through the definition and its closed interface TypeSpec",
      "True self/mutual TypeSpec identity-resolution cycles retain rejection and finite work",
      "Existing invalid erased/expanding closure tests unchanged",
      "Original full native replay and existing thirty-file focused scope after root freezes corrected source"
    ],
    "authorCoordination": "clr_services separately diagnosed the SFCLR008 unload failure as an invalid test expectation: dependency assembly was not accepted before unload, so subsequent new resolution must reject. No unload product change proposed by this reviewer.",
    "atomicIntegration": "Constraint composition WIP stays separate. Port the accepted marker fix only after root owns a new upstream correction commit; frozen5be untouched."
  },
